  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rehabilitation of agricultural land</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">War-affected agricultural lands are mapped and prioritized where there is suspected and/or actual presence of mines and Explosive Remnants of War (ERW).

Activity: Selection, identification and geospatial analysis of target areas. 
FAO and its technical partners will systematically identify and map agricultural areas most impacted by the conflict in the Dnipropetrovska oblast. This involves a comprehensive geospatial analysis that integrates satellite imagery and field data to establish a land use baseline and categorize the extent of warfare damage, such as craters and soil degradation. The resulting maps, data layers and satellite imagery provide a critical evidence base to visualize the impact on agriculture, prioritize areas for demining and soil restoration, and effectively target livelihood support to the most vulnerable small-scale farmers. 

The project is based on a gender sensitive approach and data are collected disaggregated by gender, age and disability, ensuring gender-sensitive and inclusive access to financial services.</narrative>
  </description>
